{"title":"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Video_Solution_by_Math_Is_Special)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Video Solution by Math Is Special)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b43768913fd5dd350a34daf1051839ef19642053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Z$\" width=\"11\" height=\"12\" /> be the set of integers, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/5/3059061e1536328c07a539866221deea3230c662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f\\colon \\mathbb Z \\to \\mathbb Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> be a function. Prove that there are infinitely many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec81882e66206bdcbcb4bb698f4490fc05156ee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g\\colon \\mathbb Z \\to \\mathbb Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed936cf81a055e05e4d604b01efc779eac23644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = f(x) + cx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" /> is not bijective. Note: A function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec81882e66206bdcbcb4bb698f4490fc05156ee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g\\colon \\mathbb Z \\to \\mathbb Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> is bijective if for every integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, there exists exactly one integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/cebe135d40a77f78a0bbd9ddf20d9aff3d47bb4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a) = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f2a2c0efda39d82a8d664e6c6632d070ea9d9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=f(a)-f(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /> makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/0/b9031ac4612862975ed234056194e556134086b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a)=g(a+1),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> so for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f2a2c0efda39d82a8d664e6c6632d070ea9d9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=f(a)-f(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is not bijective. If there are infinitely many possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421dbe5ac249bea2c9d25145a7eb9b73644c5c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> we are done. Otherwise, there are only finitely many possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/3693712d34e3b5618249908dfda829835b1b7a17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)-f(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> so there are only finitely many possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f531d63a5c55b304a4f8d9ff61cbef1020673a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(f(a)-f(a+1))=f(a+1)-f(a).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"305\" height=\"20\" /> This means there is a minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/629d6898d4ab996d54982e20bd34e643744f9695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a+1)-f(a).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" /> It is clear for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e28efa00c4f2c66d1aa381c0cb1f8e0ef8d6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5603715ad543a98d8baedcdb85323d69b763b544.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=f(0)+\\sum_{a=0}^{x-1}(f(a+1)-f(a))\\ge dx+f(0)\\]\" width=\"376\" height=\"50\" />\nand for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f49c02156182b52e194d0186a4e45adde6cea29.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=f(0)-\\sum_{a=x}^{-1}\\le dx+f(0).\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"50\" />\nThen, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f687d1ed816da9dee7a3909bd411d48f7afb735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;-d+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" /> be an integer. We have for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462aac924ab22435d2e3baf16c66ef01ab8c2e23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fddb63cb1b715bf1c66330657b961abf54d6437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/4006891c57e4154faf3fced75c68e293ebcf24dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(x)=f(x)+cx\\ge (d+c)x+f(0)&gt;3x+f(0)&gt;3+f(0),\\]\" width=\"472\" height=\"18\" />\nif <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615d44a736728dc026aa17d4b9c9e54a882e4f9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=f(0),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" /> and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6ee9e1d469aaf9877395fb25844dde5cbfc77cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(x)=f(x)+cx\\le (d+c)x+f(0)&lt;3x+f(0)&lt;f(0).\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"18\" />\nThis means that there is no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9fc4a3f0f6e8f1335fa041b4ad6223b0b351e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a)=f(0)+1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is not bijective.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~BS2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_2\">Proof 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/6168254a05f936dd2a0195357d1b572e7b0bd091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = f(a) - f(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bb1662a9b1947168300e567dae88b197f616072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a) = g(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />, which is not injective, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not bijective. We provide another approach.\n</p><p>Let there exist infinitely many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. This is possible if one considers all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c868fe7793542106d2ed5336b54efc68d97ec0ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />, so we are done.\n</p><p>If there are only finitely many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, then we prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be surjective, and therefore not bijective. That is, all sets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd774c02728a7dc8c4ef0c7342416693fd2c1557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\in \\{d_{\\min}, \\dots, d_{\\max} \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />. Choose a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/6721ce06e9dd5f6d02e7f9c8affeae1ee99d778d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = M+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c07feb324a385ae5871df6f381d2117056bc281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = d_{\\max}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />. Then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09e666be7b5faf58c52ff7e4a671f06e0ad0bc83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(a+1) - g(a) = f(a+1)-f(a) + c\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1189cf01c755f4501808f42bc6f7934c54788be2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=-d_{\\max} + c\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/5425174d8ef909dbd1b06334383353ac65d87b8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\geq 1\\]\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>which is viable. However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/193c5bccb777ec38a10ed275d176b0c7112a9ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &gt; M+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09e666be7b5faf58c52ff7e4a671f06e0ad0bc83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(a+1) - g(a) = f(a+1)-f(a) + c\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1189cf01c755f4501808f42bc6f7934c54788be2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=-d_{\\max} + c\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d47fe64cbe46ba391949d96a82be8e79800bd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\geq 2\\]\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Which is indeed not surjective and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not bijective.\n</p><p>The proof is complete. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Video_Solution_by_Math_Is_Special.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Video_Solution_by_Math_Is_Special)\">Solution 3 (Video Solution by Math Is Special)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Video Solution by Math Is Special)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nLLVICtnoyM\">https://youtu.be/nLLVICtnoyM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO\" title=\"2025 USAJMO\">2025 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033514\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 312/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9474/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.677      1 -total\n 72.37%   13.516      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 25.99%    4.854      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31356:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018033514 and revision id 293776. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}